│ patch_description        │ Test reducing relocation to two particles when recent improvement covers at least one     │
│                          │ quarter of the observed loss in the larger-radius regime. Retained velocities and         │
│                          │ refreshed memories may let ordinary PSO motion contribute enough recovery to justify      │
│                          │ relocating fewer particles.                                                               │
│                          │ Doubling recovery credit previously reduced mean offline error from 3.26 to 3.23,         │
│                          │ although individual cases worsened. Case_013 improved from 3.0421 to 2.2584, with         │
│                          │ interval-end error falling from 1.0833 to 0.4625. Executed count-two responses remained   │
│                          │ uncommon, and detection overhead stayed near 16%. This motivates testing a broader        │
│                          │ threshold, without assuming that more frequent count-two allocation will improve          │
│                          │ performance. The proposed multiplier is untested.                                         │
