│ patch_description        │ Combine the tighter contraction threshold at smaller default radii with the broader       │
│                          │ threshold at larger radii. The tighter parent improved case_001 error from 3.371 to       │
│                          │ 2.874; the broader parent improved case_010 from 5.769 to 5.193 and interval-end error    │
│                          │ from 3.442 to 2.741. Executed distributions confirm both parents used three and four      │
│                          │ relocations, with the broader threshold generally increasing four-count responses. Retain │
│                          │ their shared loss-versus-improvement condition. This tests whether the useful contraction │
│                          │ threshold depends on the public radius scale; improved aggregate performance remains      │
│                          │ unmeasured.                                                                               │
