│ patch_description        │ Test an eightfold recovery-credit threshold in the larger-radius regime. The twofold and  │
│                          │ fourfold variants both reduced mean offline error from approximately 3.26 to 3.23, while  │
│                          │ still executing count three on most responses. This motivates testing a broader           │
│                          │ opportunity for count two, preserving ordinary PSO motion in three particles.             │
│                          │ The evidence is mixed: case_013 improved substantially, but case_008 worsened, and        │
│                          │ case_009 retained substantial interval-end error. This proposal tests whether broader     │
│                          │ partial relocation helps overall; it does not establish that historical progress predicts │
│                          │ recovery. Detection and memory reevaluation costs remain unchanged, and performance       │
│                          │ requires measurement.                                                                     │
