│ patch_description        │ Use three relocations by default and four when the swarm diameter is below the actual     │
│                          │ relocation radius and fitness loss exceeds recent improvement. The radius is twice        │
│                          │ default_radius.                                                                           │
│                          │ The previous conditional rules achieved mean errors 3.19 and 3.16 versus 3.28 for         │
│                          │ constant four. Broadening the contraction threshold improved case_010 from 5.768937 to    │
│                          │ 5.193272, with interval-end error falling from 3.44168 to 2.74066, although case_011      │
│                          │ worsened. Executed counts confirm that both conditional rules mixed three and four        │
│                          │ relocations; detection overhead remained near 16%.                                        │
│                          │ This proposal tests whether the broader, dimensionless contraction threshold also helps   │
│                          │ at smaller movement scales. It retains ordinary PSO motion for more particles when the    │
│                          │ swarm already spans the relocation radius or recent progress offsets the observed loss.   │
│                          │ Improvement remains an untested hypothesis.                                               │
